            "review_title": "Review at Sushi Sakura",
            "review_text": "jemsgibb\nMelbourne, Australia34 contributions\n0\nNot coming back\nNov 2018 • Couples\nMy partner and I came here last night for dinner. We walked in at 7pm,ordered three dishes by 7:05. We waited 50 MINUTES for one plate of sushi, and another 5 mins for the next plate, which were both my partners so I was still hungry. I didn't get my food until I alerted the staff I had been waiting an hour and ten minutes for it (it was a small bento box...). So my partner finished his food before I even got mine, and we did not get to eat our food together. By this point I was just hungry and tired so the meal wasn't enjoyable. \n\nI was given some excuse that they only had one sushi chef that day. However, there were only three other tables in the restaurant and they already had their food, so I'm not sure why it took one sushi chef an hour to put together a bento box with a couple sushi rolls, ngiri, and tempura prawn. The staff did not even apologise for this. Furthermore, they could have alerted us before we sat down that the food was going to take a very long time. I also did see more than one chef behind the curtain, so I'm not sure if that's the whole truth or just trying to cover themselves for forgetting about our food. \n\nThe food itself lacked flavour and wasn't the best quality. \n\nI will definitely NOT be coming back and don't recommend anyone else do either.\nRead more\nWritten November 22, 2018",
